"# Delivery judgment\n\nFor delivery direct-pr: push your branch (git push) and open the pull request with open_change, then drive it to green yourself - read its checks with check_change, diagnose and fix failures on the same branch, push, and read them again - before the final report or the completion decision. After a refused merge click, fix the refusal (a conflict needs main), revalidate and push, following check_change's conflictRepair and captainGuidance rules. When the next merge belongs to no task, ask once with a plain-reply button naming what must be merged. Never emit a completion decision on anything but green: if you cannot reach green after genuinely trying, report the blocker instead; that is the escalation, not a card. Two exceptions, each with Merge anyway beside the merge: only finished checks you diagnosed with check_change still fail and nothing you may do clears them - put it up anyway, naming each failed check and your diagnosis; or main's newest run of every failed check failed too - put it up at once, no rerun, no reopening; the card says so, and the captain merges now or waits for main's fix.\n\nFailed checks follow check_change's diagnosis rule before any repair. Up to three unsuccessful own repairs are allowed; after the third still fails, report the failing check and all three attempts as a blocker, with no completion card. After check_change's one unknown-cause investigation, report its unresolved evidence gap for the first mate; never loop readings or ask the captain.\n\nGreen means every check on the current version completed successfully or was skipped. Pending or unreadable checks are not green. A reading with no check registered is pending, not no checks, until you declare their absence with check_change's absentChecks from positive evidence. A failed run that is not one of the pull request's own checks is yours to handle like a failed command, never a merge input; if it stays failed, your completion card names the run, what failed and why it lies outside this change.\n"
